Consider the following snippet of a C program. Assume that swap (&x, &y) exchanges the
contents of x and y.<pre><code>
int main ( ) {
int array[]={3,5,1,4,6,2};
int done =0 ;
int i ;
while (done == 0) {
   done = 1;
   for (i = 0; i <=4; i ++) {
   if (array [i] < array [i +1]) {
       swap (& array [i], &array [i+1]);
       done = 0;
    }
}
for (i = 5 ; i &gt;=1; i --) {
if (array [i] > array [ i-1]) {
    swap ( & array [i] , &array [i-1]);
     done = 0;
  }
} }
printf ( " %d " , array [3] );
}</code></pre>
The output of the program is ____________.

